      "content": "It is likely dangerous to take tramadol without a prescription, as sudden interactions with sertraline can lower your seizure threshold or cause serotonin syndrome, even at low doses. Combining these medications without medical supervision can disrupt your medication's half-life and obscure how your body is reacting to the pain relief. Please take a few deep breaths and try heating packs or gentle stretching before sleeping tonight; over the next few hours, contact a local clinic or pharmacy to ask for a paper prescription or emergency consultation.",
